  "question": {
    "text": "A missile is fired from the ground level rises \\(x\\) meters vertically upwards in \\(t \\sec\\), where \\(x=100 t-\\frac{25}{2} t^2\\). The maximum height reached is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "76kXT",
      "text": "\\(100 \\mathrm{~m}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qeIv3",
      "text": "\\(300 \\mathrm{~m}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fKLIB",
      "text": "\\(200 \\mathrm{~m}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JV1qp",
      "text": "\\(125 \\mathrm{~m}\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(x=100 t-\\frac{25}{2} t^2\\)\n\\(\\frac{d x}{d t}=100-25 \\mathrm{t}\\) for maximum and minimum \\(\\frac{d x}{d t}=0 \\Rightarrow t=4 \\mathrm{sec}\\)\n\\(\\frac{d^2 x}{d t^2}=-25  < 0\\)\n\\(\\therefore\\) at \\(\\mathrm{x}=4\\) it will have maixmum height\n\\(x_{\\max }=100 \\times 4-\\frac{25}{2} \\times 16=400-200=200 \\mathrm{~m}\\)",
    "image": null
